{
  "evidence": "The agent correctly located the target YouTube video and called the appropriate youtube-transcript-get_transcript tool to extract lyrics. However, the request was immediately rejected by YouTube because the agent's datacenter IP was flagged by anti-bot protections. A subsequent fallback attempt using a browser tool was blocked by the same IP-based bot wall, forcing the agent to extract incorrect decoy songs from the video description.",
  "reasoning": "The root cause is not a model or tool error, as the agent formed a correct plan, selected the right tool, and even attempted a logical fallback strategy. The failure was strictly caused by the external destination (YouTube) imposing a persistent, non-recoverable block on the agent's datacenter IP. This matches the definition of a Service Failure where an external service abruptly terminates the request and prevents any legitimate path to the data.",
  "category": "env (external) — model",
  "subtype": "Service Failure"
}
